# Shell scripts must be LF in the index. A CRLF shebang is "bad interpreter" on
# Linux, and every one of these runs on a Pi. This is not hypothetical: an
# editor pass normalised install.sh to CRLF, which would have broken the first
# fresh clone and the SD image build with it.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Systemd units and the CI workflow are read by Linux tooling too.
*.service text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
